Unified capture pipeline across all the astro cameras — built by wrapping the per-camera work, not absorbing it.

The capture / acquisition layer of the astro estate: the *unified* pipeline that turns "a camera pointed at the sky" into frames on disk, across every instrument (astro-polecam, astro-eclipticam, astro-canon). It owns the common machinery — capture scheduling, night/session structure, frame naming and hand-off to storage — as distinct from the per-device specifics (which live in each [[astro-canon]]-style camera keeper) and from the downstream processing/science (which lives in [[astro-science]]). Three-layer split: astro-<camera> = device specifics, astro-capture = unified capture, astro-science = pipeline + deliverables. The pipeline is assembled **from** the camera-specific work by wrapping it, so what is genuinely unified is the *conventions* (run-tagged stems, one capture = one frame, session structure) rather than a single code path — a gphoto2 DSLR and a picamera2 Pi share the former and cannot share the latter.
